  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A short feedback prompt asks about game choice, ease of joining, and anything that made participation difficult; answering is optional.\", \"decision\": \"How should guests suggest improvements for the next evening?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nGuests complete the short feedback prompt as they leave and place it in a collection box. Immediate impressions are captured privately before details of joining games and understanding the evening begin to fade.\nThe host sends the short feedback prompt the following day and groups replies before planning another evening. Guests have time to reflect, and the organizer can compare recurring experiences across people who played different games.\nA volunteer offers departing guests a brief conversation using the feedback prompt and records comments without names. People can explain a difficulty in their own words while the same questions keep responses useful for later planning."
    }
  ],
